ustrial products. The utilization of these&#10;compounds in the field of organic electronics is reviewed&#10;with particular emphasis on organic field-effect&#10;transistors. It is shown that for most major classes of&#10;industrial dye...&#10;&#10;20. Color chemistry syntheses properties and applications&#10;of organic dyes and pigments (1987)&#10;Abstract: Introduction Color of Organic Compounds Polyene&#10;and Polymethine Dyes Di- and Triarylmethine Dyes and their&#10;Aza Analogues Aza[18]annulenes Nitro and Nitroso Dyes Azo&#10;Dyes and Pigments Carbonyl Dyes and Pigments Sulfur Dyes&#10;Fluorescent Brighteners Application of Dyes Application..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2400" y="1304" width="442" height="3444" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_event_2" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;dashed=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step1" target="retrieval_2"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_3" value="Retrieval 3&#10;step: step2&#10;command: openalex&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 10&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;source: openalex&#10;query: GENERATING RESEARCH QUESTIONS THROUGH&#10;PROBLEMATIZATION.&#10;direction: backward&#10;node_id: https://openalex.org/W2099043095&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Archaeology of Knowledge (1970)&#10;Abstract: In France, a country that awards its&#10;intellectuals the status other countries give their rock&#10;stars, Michel Foucault was part of a glittering generation&#10;of thinkers, one which also included Sartre, de Beauvoir&#10;and Deleuze. One of the great intellectual heroes of the&#10;twentieth...&#10;&#10;2. Outline of a Theory of Practice (2007)&#10;Abstract: Outline of a Theory of Practice is recognized as&#10;a major theoretical text on the foundations of&#10;anthropology and sociology. Pierre Bourdieu, a&#10;distinguished French anthropologist, develops a theory of&#10;practice which is simultaneously a critique of the methods&#10;and postures of s...&#10;&#10;3. Feminist practice and poststructuralist theory (1988)&#10;Abstract: Acknowledgements. Preface to the Second Edition.&#10;1. Feminism and Theory. 2. Principles of&#10;Poststructuralism. 3. Feminist Poststructuralism and&#10;Psychoanalysis. 4. Language and Subjectivity. 5.&#10;Discourse, Power and Resistance. 6. Feminist Critical&#10;Practice. 7. Feminism and Postm...&#10;&#10;4. Ambiguity and Choice in Organizations. (1977)&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;5. Engaged Scholarship: A Guide for Organizational and&#10;Social Research (2007)&#10;Abstract: 1. Engaged Scholarship in a Professional School&#10;2. Philosophy of Science Underlying Engaged Scholarship 3.&#10;Formulating the Research Problem 4. Building a Theory 5.&#10;Process and Variance Models 6. Designing Variance Studies&#10;7. Designing Process Studies 8. Communicating and Using...&#10;&#10;6. Science of Science and Reflexivity (2004)&#10;Abstract: Over the last four decades, the French&#10;sociologist Pierre Bourdieu produced one of the most&#10;imaginative and subtle bodies of social theory of the&#10;postwar era. When he died in 2002, he was considered to be&#10;a thinker on a par with Foucault, Barthes, and Lacan a&#10;public intellectu...&#10;&#10;7. Occupational Communities: Culture and Control in&#10;Organizations (1982)&#10;Abstract: Abstract : The organization is but one frame of&#10;reference for understanding work behavior. Equally&#10;powerful but largely unexplored social forces in the&#10;workplace are groups sired by the perception of common&#10;task. After developing the concept of an occupational&#10;community as a f...&#10;&#10;8. Explaining Organizational Behavior. (1983)&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;9. Tricks of the Trade: How to Think about Your Research&#10;While You're Doing It (1998)&#10;Abstract: Tricks of the Trade will help students think&#10;about research projects. Assisted by Becker's sound&#10;advice, students will be able to make better sense of&#10;their research and simultaneously generate fresh ideas on&#10;where to look next for new data. Becker's tricks cover&#10;four broad ar...&#10;&#10;10. The use of pleasure (1990)&#10;Abstract: Part 1 Introduction: modifications forms of&#10;problematization morality and practice of the self. Part 2&#10;The moral problematization of pleasures: Aphrodisia&#10;Chresis Enkrateia freedom and truth. Part 3 Dietetics:&#10;regimen in general the diet of pleasures risks and dangers&#10;act, exp..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2400" y="4788" width="442" height="1716" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_event_3" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;dashed=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step2" target="retrieval_3"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_4" value="Retrieval 4&#10;step: step2&#10;command: openalex&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 10&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;source: openalex&#10;query: GENERATING RESEARCH QUESTIONS THROUGH&#10;PROBLEMATIZATION.&#10;direction: forward&#10;node_id: https://openalex.org/W2099043095&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Designing conceptual articles: four approaches (2020)&#10;Abstract: Abstract As a powerful means of theory building,&#10;conceptual articles are increasingly called for in&#10;marketing academia. However, researchers struggle to&#10;design and write non-empirical articles because of the&#10;lack of commonly accepted templates to guide their&#10;development. The a...&#10;&#10;2. “Systematic combining”—A decade later (2013)&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;3. A Hermeneutic Approach for Conducting Literature&#10;Reviews and Literature Searches (2014)&#10;Abstract: The quality and success of scholarly work&#10;depends in large measure on the quality of the literature&#10;review process. This paper advances conceptual&#10;understanding of the literature review process and extends&#10;earlier guidelines on literature reviews. It proposes a&#10;hermeneutic fra...&#10;&#10;4. Unlocking the circular economy through new business&#10;models based on large-scale data: An integrative framework&#10;and research agenda (2017)&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;5. Artificial intelligence for supply chain resilience:&#10;learning from Covid-19 (2021)&#10;Abstract: Purpose Many supply chains have faced disruption&#10;during Covid-19. Artificial intelligence (AI) is one&#10;mechanism that can be used to improve supply chain&#10;resilience by developing business continuity capabilities.&#10;This study examines how firms employ AI and consider the&#10;opportun...&#10;&#10;6. What literature review is not: diversity, boundaries&#10;and recommendations (2014)&#10;Abstract: In Orlando the EJIS Board decided to implement a&#10;policy change that I had proposed in my last editorial&#10;addressing the IS community (Rowe, 2012), asking authors&#10;(starting January 2013) to explicitl...&#10;&#10;7. A Stupidity‐Based Theory of Organizations (2012)&#10;Abstract: abstract In this paper we question the one‐sided&#10;thesis that contemporary organizations rely on the&#10;mobilization of cognitive capacities. We suggest that&#10;severe restrictions on these capacities in the form of&#10;what we call functional stupidity are an equally important&#10;if under‐...&#10;&#10;8. Has Management Studies Lost Its Way? Ideas for More&#10;Imaginative and Innovative Research (2012)&#10;Abstract: abstract Despite the huge increase in the number&#10;of management articles published during the three last&#10;decades, there is a serious shortage of high‐impact&#10;research in management studies. We contend that a primary&#10;reason behind this paradoxical shortage is the near total&#10;domin...&#10;&#10;9. Supply chain agility, adaptability and alignment (2017)&#10;Abstract: Purpose The purpose of this paper is to examine&#10;when and how organizations create agility, adaptability,&#10;and alignment as distinct supply chain properties to gain&#10;sustainable competitive advantage.&#10;Design/methodology/approach The current study utilizes the&#10;resource-based view...&#10;&#10;10. Critical leadership studies: The case for critical&#10;performativity (2012)&#10;Abstract: Existing accounts of leadership are underpinned&#10;by two dominant approaches: functionalist studies, which&#10;have tried to identify correlations between variables&#10;associated with leadership; and interpretive studies,&#10;which have tried to trace out the meaning-making process&#10;associa..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2400" y="6544" width="442" height="1806" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_event_4" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;dashed=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step2" target="retrieval_4"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_5" value="Retrieval 5&#10;step: step6&#10;command: paper-search&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 1&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: Current pigment discovery remains largely&#10;empirical and serendipitous because there is no robust&#10;predictive and inverse design framework that jointly links&#10;chemical composition, crystal structure, electronic&#10;structure, defect chemistry, particle morphology,&#10;synthesis feasibility, stability, toxicity, and perceived&#10;color to identify practically useful new pigments.&#10;field: abstract&#10;top_k: 1&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. The Serendipitous Discovery of a Rose Odorant (2020)&#10;[score=0.5475938320159912]&#10;Abstract: Serendipity has played a role in many&#10;groundbreaking scientific discoveries. Key to their&#10;identification and exploitation is the ability to&#10;recognize the unexpected and invest time trying to&#10;understand it. Like any other field of scientific&#10;research, total synthesis requires d..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2400" y="8390" width="442" height="510" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_event_5" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;dashed=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step6" target="retrieval_5"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_6" value="Retrieval 6&#10;step: step6&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 1&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: Apply generative inverse design and multi-&#10;objective optimization methods, such as graph neural&#10;networks, Bayesian optimization, and active learning, to&#10;propose candidate pigment compositions that satisfy target&#10;color, stability, toxicity, and synthesis constraints.&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'generative inverse design', 'score':&#10;9}, {'text': 'multi-objective optimization', 'score': 8},&#10;{'text': 'graph neural networks', 'score': 8}, {'text':&#10;'active learning', 'score': 7}, {'text': 'Bayesian&#10;optimization', 'score': 7}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 1&#10;retrieval_mode: semantic&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Enhancing Paint Formula Innovation Using Generative AI&#10;and Historical Data Analytics (2025) [score=1.0]&#10;Abstract: This work implements a generative artificial&#10;intelligence approach and a search algorithm to recreate&#10;and innovate paint formulas on a hardware-near level. We&#10;use clustering techniques to explore data latent space and&#10;then implement Markov Chain Monte Carlo techniques to&#10;sampl..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="2400" y="8940" width="442" height="600" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_event_6" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;dashed=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step6" target="retrieval_6"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>